==English==
[[File:Oreochromis-niloticus-Nairobi.JPG|alt=A side view of a fish|thumb|right|Nile '''tilapia''', ''Oreochromis niloticus'']]
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|mul|Tilapia}}, from {{der|en|tn|tlhapi||fish}}.
The drag race slang usage is a reference to the comment by Gia Gunn on entering Ru Paul's Drag Race (season 6) "Just landed like fresh tilapia".

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/təˈlɑːpiə/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/tɪˈlɑːpiə/|/tɪˈlæpiə/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tilapia.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːpiə|æpiə}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|tilapia}}

# Any of various [[edible]] [[fish]], formerly species of the [[genus]] {{taxfmt|Tilapia|genus}}, but now placed in other [[cichlid]] genera (such as {{taxlink|Oreochromis|genus}}), native to [[Africa]] and the [[Middle East]] but cultivated [[worldwide]].
#: {{syn|en|St. Peter's fish}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2006|author=w:Tom Waits; w:Kathleen Brennan|title=Bottom of the World|passage=Well I dined last night with Scarface Ron<br>On '''tilapia''' fishcakes and fried black swan.}}
# {{lb|en|Drag Race slang}} A [[fishy]] {{gloss|resembling a cisgender woman}} [[drag queen]]; a drag queen who could pass for a woman, as opposed to one who is exaggeratedly feminine.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Sam Damshenas|title=Drag Race star Plastique Tiara wants to be a "pioneer" for the queer Asian community|work=w:Gay Times|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210801165815/https://www.gaytimes.co.uk/culture/drag-race-star-plastique-tiara-wants-to-be-a-pioneer-for-the-queer-asian-community/|location=London|publisher=Gay Times Ltd|date=13 June 2019|issn=0950-6101|oclc=303044001|passage=Vietnamese '''tilapia''' Plastique Tiara was at the forefront of one of Drag Race's most controversial eliminations earlier this year. Although the Texan performer and biological woman was leaving us gooped week-after-week with her runways, she was – spoiler alert! – eliminated in eighth place after lip-syncing against Miss Vanjie, despite having a better track record.}}

